  "notes": "Excellent food, lively conversation, a busy dining room — and a sound level that made relaxing surprisingly difficult.\n\nThis SPL Reference measurement was taken during dinner in a Turkish restaurant, where conversations, music, service and the reflections of many simultaneous voices combined into a dense and energetic soundscape.\n\nNothing was necessarily wrong with the atmosphere; the restaurant was simply very lively. Yet it raises an interesting question: at what point does a vibrant restaurant become acoustically tiring?\n\nA reminder that our experience of a restaurant is shaped not only by what is on the plate, but also by the environment in which we enjoy it.",
